      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Conventionally casting equiatomic CoCrFeMnNi produces a coarse-grained state.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The initial CoCrFeMnNi alloy is a single-phase solid solution.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12388374::web::001::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The baseline CoCrFeMnNi alloy has established high ductility and fracture toughness.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12388374::web::001::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The baseline ductility and toughness arise from its uniform single-phase microstructure.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "High-pressure torsion produces an ultrafine-grained microstructure in CoCrFeMnNi.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12388374::web::001::1_introduction",
        "PMC12388374::web::018::3_2_mechanical_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "High-pressure torsion increases the density and proportion of high-angle grain boundaries in CoCrFeMnNi.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Decreasing grain size increases strength through Hall–Petch behavior.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5075899::web::006::compressive_stress_strain_behavior_of_bu"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "A high density of grain boundaries can impede dislocation glide.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12388374::web::018::3_2_mechanical_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "High-angle grain boundaries localize stress and act as crack-initiation sites under mechanical loading.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Boundary-induced stress localization and inhibited homogeneous dislocation motion promote brittle crack nucleation and override possible toughness benefits from grain refinement.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The HPT-processed alloy will have lower fracture toughness than the coarse-grained as-cast alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The HPT-processed alloy will exhibit a transition toward more brittle fracture, with earlier crack initiation at or near high-angle grain boundaries.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The detrimental grain-boundary effect will be most pronounced at high strain rates and elevated temperatures.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed mechanism applies to severe dynamic loading in aerospace and high-performance automotive service.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A controlled test compares coarse-grained cast and HPT-processed CoCrFeMnNi using identical tensile and fracture-toughness tests while measuring grain size, high-angle-boundary fraction, and crack locations.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.design",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Failure to observe either a statistically significant toughness reduction or preferential cracking at high-angle grain boundaries would falsify the proposed mechanism.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.falsification_rule",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
